@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper a ds:Component;
    ds:name "TooltipWrapper";
    ds:summary "The wrapper tooltip is a flexible tooltip designed to support richer content beyond a single line of text. It is best suited for use cases where multiple content types must be supported, such as text, KVPs ([KVPItem (base)](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-eUn6xQeQ6l)), or tables. This type of tooltip is ideal when standard tooltips are too limited, but a modal or larger surface would feel too disruptive. \n\nRelated to [Tooltip](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-ONb9LwkGvW) and [TooltipData](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-Y1ha3zI_b_).";
    ds:anatomyDsl "---\n# The tooltip for structured content: its body is a slot for any components.\n# Content colour is set by the slotted components, so none is bound here. An\n# inverted wrapper is made by switching the variable mode of the instance, so\n# the colours are bound directly and not through surface channels.\nnode:\n  uri: global.component.tooltip_wrapper\n  styles:\n    layout.type: flex\n    layout.direction: column\n    layout.align: flex-start\n    # Stays visible so the arrow, which sits outside the box, is not clipped.\n    layout.overflow: visible\n    appearance.background: color.background.container\n    appearance.border.color: color.border.muted\n    appearance.border.style: solid\n    appearance.border.width: dimension.stroke.thickness.medium\n    appearance.radius: dimension.radius.small\n    spacing.gap: dimension.100\n    spacing.internal.block.start: dimension.200\n    spacing.internal.block.end: dimension.200\n    spacing.internal.inline.start: dimension.200\n    spacing.internal.inline.end: dimension.200\n  edges:\n    - switch:\n        on: override\n        cases:\n          - uri: $custom\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"0..*\"\n        slotName: default\n    - node:\n        role: arrow\n        styles:\n          layout.position: absolute\n          # Which side it points from follows the Arrow variant, so its offsets\n          # are not bound, and the DSL has no triangle shape. The variant also\n          # adds 8px of padding on the arrow side, which the tree cannot carry\n          # per variant.\n          size.width: dimension.175\n          size.height: dimension.100\n          appearance.background: color.background.container\n          appearance.border.color: color.border.muted\n          appearance.border.style: solid\n          appearance.border.width: dimension.stroke.thickness.medium\n      relation:\n        # The component draws the arrow; no caller fills it, so it carries no\n        # slot name.\n        cardinality: \"1\"";
    ds:anatomyClassic "## Anatomy\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=13993-2495&t=pA5l7Omuxa3ATwVS-1\n\n1. **Container**\n\nA content slot. No max width.\n\n1. **Slot content**\n\nAnything non-interactive: free text, a chart legend, a key-value list, a tooltip table or a Pragma component. Default is a placeholder.\n\n1. **Arrow** **(optional)**\n\nPoints from the tooltip to its trigger.\n\n**Helper components**\n\n- **Chart legend item**: one legend row with marker, label, optional value, and a rule below. State: Default or Highlighted (hovered series).\n- **Chart legend**: heading plus a slot of legend items. Turn Show rule off on the last item.\n- **Key-value pair**: Inline (value right-aligned) or Stacked. Strong is bold; use it as a group header.\n- **Key-value list**: a slot of key-value pairs. Width is set per instance.\n- **Tooltip table and row**: compact table with an exposed header row plus a slot of body rows. Two, three or four equal-width columns.\n- **Series marker**: 6 x 6 circle. Override the fill per series.\n- **Slot placeholder**: default content of the Wrapper slot. Replace it.\n\n## Styling\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=13993-3879&t=pA5l7Omuxa3ATwVS-1";
    ds:usage "## When to use\n\n- When tooltip content requires internal structure such as tables, key–value pairs, legends, or media\n- When used in dashboards or data-heavy contexts requiring quick, glanceable detail\n- When flexibility is required without introducing multiple bespoke tooltip variants\n\n## When not to use\n\n- When only simple icon or control clarification is needed\n  - Incorrect: A wrapper tooltip is used for a single short label explanation\n  - Remediation: Use a [Standard tooltip](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20chnVyhaz/_rui-Y9PpN4FiwA) or [Dense tooltip](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20chnVyhaz/_rui-tES05lAnIw) \n- When content must persist or be interactive\n  - Incorrect: A wrapper tooltip contains controls or actions\n  - Remediation: Use a [Popover](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-i-62pvfoOF) or [Modal](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-XsokbPLmnc) \n- When only a single short sentence is required\n  - Incorrect: A wrapper tooltip is used for minimal text\n  - Remediation: Use a [Standard tooltip](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20chnVyhaz/_rui-Y9PpN4FiwA) \n- When the element is already clearly labelled or self-explanatory.\n\n**In essence:**\n\nWhen in doubt, start with standard [Tooltip](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-ONb9LwkGvW). Move to its [Tooltip+Dense](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-PFE_wK_bWT) variant for space constraints; [TooltipWrapper](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-69TNyYt7M9) for structured content and complex hierarchies; [TooltipData](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-Y1ha3zI_b_) for data visualization.";
    ds:guidelines "- Show with a 400 ms delay after hover or focus\n- Hide with a 400 ms delay after the pointer leaves\n- Cancel display if the pointer exits before the show delay completes\n- If the pointer moves directly from one tooltip trigger to another, show the new tooltip immediately and skip the previous tooltip’s exit animation\n\n### **Transition**\n\n- **Type**: spring\n- **Duration**: 0.4 s\n- **Bounce**: 0.2\n- **Delay**: 0 s\n\n### Reduced motion\n\n- Fade in and out with no scale or movement, keeping the same delays.\n\n### CSS fallback\n\n- Opacity 0 to 1 and scale 0.96 to 1 over 400 ms, cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1), transform origin at the arrow.\n\n### Interactions\n\n- Opens on hover and on keyboard focus, never on click.\n- Closes when the pointer or focus leaves, on Escape, and when another tooltip opens.\n- Only one tooltip is open at a time.\n- The pointer can move onto the tooltip without it closing.\n- Slot content stays non-interactive.\n\n### Positioning and responsive\n\n- Positioned relative to its trigger, centred with an 8 px offset. Flips to the opposite side when there isn't enough room and never overflows the viewport.\n- Collision padding is 24 px.\n- Tooltips don't appear on touch devices, so essential information must be available another way.\n\n### Typography\n\n- Helper headings and Strong key-value pairs: typography-text-secondary-$bold. Tooltip table headers: typography-text-tertiary-$bold.\n- Values use tabular figures in code.\n\n### Keyboard support\n\n- Tab or Shift+Tab to a trigger opens its tooltip.\n- Escape closes it without moving focus.\n\n### Focus\n\n- Tooltips aren't focusable and aren't part of the tab order.\n- A disabled control that needs an explanation should be wrapped in a focusable element.\n\n### ARIA\n\n- The tooltip element has role=\"tooltip\", and the trigger references it with aria-describedby.\n- Decorative icons inside the tooltip are hidden from assistive technology.";
    ds:tier ds:global;
    ds:documentationStage ds:tag.needsfulldocumentation;
    ds:hasProperty [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "***Wrapper tooltip***";
        ds:optional "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "*Wrapper container*";
        ds:optional "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "Position";
        ds:summary "Preferred placement relative to trigger";
        ds:optional "false";
        ds:propertyType "choice"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "Max width";
        ds:summary "Optional width override for wrapper tooltip";
        ds:optional "false";
        ds:propertyType "number"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "*Wrapper item*";
        ds:optional "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "Wrapper item (instance swap)";
        ds:summary "Selects which content block appears in this wrapper row";
        ds:optional "false";
        ds:propertyType "element"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "*Key-value pair* (when selected as wrapper item)";
        ds:optional "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "Value structure";
        ds:summary "Whether value is single or multi-entry";
        ds:optional "false";
        ds:propertyType "choice"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "Value layout";
        ds:summary "How value is arranged visually";
        ds:optional "false";
        ds:propertyType "choice"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "Layout";
        ds:summary "Layout control. Not for users.";
        ds:optional "false";
        ds:propertyType "choice"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "***All variants***";
        ds:optional "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "Type";
        ds:summary "Selects the tooltip variant";
        ds:optional "false";
        ds:propertyType "choice"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "Surrounding UI theme";
        ds:summary "Sets tooltip theme based on surrounding UI context";
        ds:optional "false";
        ds:propertyType "choice"
    ];
    ds:hasSubcomponent ds:global.subcomponent.kvp_container, ds:global.subcomponent.kvpitem_base;
    ds:hasTokenBinding [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.background";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.background.container
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.border.color";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.border.muted
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.border.width";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.stroke.thickness.medium
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.radius";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.radius.small
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "spacing.gap";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.100
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "spacing.internal.block.start";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.200
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "spacing.internal.block.end";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.200
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "spacing.internal.inline.start";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.200
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "spacing.internal.inline.end";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.200
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root/arrow";
        anatomy:styleKey "size.width";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.175
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root/arrow";
        anatomy:styleKey "size.height";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.100
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root/arrow";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.background";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.background.container
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root/arrow";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.border.color";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.border.muted
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.component.tooltip_wrapper;
        ds:node "$root/arrow";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.border.width";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.stroke.thickness.medium
    ].
